{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1496912-should-sources-of-non-silver-aggravated-damage-be-so-crippling","id":1496912,"title":"Should Sources of Non-Silver Aggravated Damage Be So Crippling?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-11-12T09:05:05-08:00","id":1496912,"title":"Should Sources of Non-Silver Aggravated Damage Be So Crippling?","content":"Maybe its for game balance purposes but isn't it kind of strange that roll over aggravated damage heals at the same rate as damage done by silver (4 days per point of aggravated, which is really close to base human)? Usually when a werewolf has a weakness to silver in most forms of media, the damage is treated as if a normal person were shot and heals at the same rates, taking weeks to recover if at all. I don't really think a werewolf should be crippled for weeks because she got back over by a bus multiple times. Wouldn't it make a bit more sense if they healed non-silver sources of aggravated damage one point per day or would that break the game? And its not like baddies who are expecting and or hunting werewolves don't bring silver along anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27672-forsakenprospects","user":"ForsakenProspects","date":". 11-12-2022, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27672-forsakenprospects","name":"ForsakenProspects","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27672_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-12T09:46:05-08:00","id":1496917,"title":"","content":"If you are a werewolf and you get into a situation where you don't have the Essence to regenerate lethal damage before it rolls over, and you can't or won't hit the panic button by shifting to Gauru, you've fucked up supremely and you can sit with the consequences by taking roughly half as long to recover as a mortal would from similar injuries.<br /> <br /> Rollover is literally the only source of aggravated damage for werewolves besides silver and supernatural powers that specifically do aggravated damage. To repeat the mantra: werewolves are hunters, not warriors \u2014 their default method of dealing with damage is regeneration and reduced susceptibility to bodily disruption so they can use hit-and-run tactics at negligible cost, not facetanking a full track of lethal damage with Armor in an all-out assault where there's a chance it'll go badly.<br /> <br /> Werewolves aren't immune to unconsciousness or bleeding out. If you've got a full track of lethal and you aren't healing it, you're down. That's your incentive to pick your battles and get going when the going gets tough unless you can make a good trade at that desperate a situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-12T10:53:29-08:00","id":1496923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1496912-should-sources-of-non-silver-aggravated-damage-be-so-crippling?p=1496917#post1496917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are a werewolf and you get into a situation where you don't have the Essence to regenerate lethal damage before it rolls over, and you can't or won't hit the panic button by shifting to Gauru, you've fucked up supremely and you can sit with the consequences by taking roughly half as long to recover as a mortal would from similar injuries.<br /> <br /> Rollover is literally the only source of aggravated damage for werewolves besides silver and supernatural powers that specifically do aggravated damage. To repeat the mantra: werewolves are hunters, not warriors \u2014 their default method of dealing with damage is regeneration and reduced susceptibility to bodily disruption so they can use hit-and-run tactics at negligible cost, not facetanking a full track of lethal damage with Armor in an all-out assault where there's a chance it'll go badly.<br /> <br /> Werewolves aren't immune to unconsciousness or bleeding out. If you've got a full track of lethal and you aren't healing it, you're down. That's your incentive to pick your battles and get going when the going gets tough unless you can make a good trade at that desperate a situation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh so like the first Predator movie (both the titular monster and the soliders). Gotcha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27672-forsakenprospects","name":"ForsakenProspects","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27672_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}